  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: 1st number **×** (1st number - 1) = 2nd number.\n\nFor, 15 ∶ 210\n\n→ 15 × (15 - 1) \n\n→ 15 × 14 = 210.\n\nNow, checking the options,\n\nOption 1) 16 ∶ 224\n\n→ 16 × (16 - 1) \n\n→ 16 × 15 = 240 ≠ 224.\n\nOption 2) 14 ∶ 196\n\n→ 14 × (14 - 1) \n\n→ 14 × 13 = 182 ≠ 196.\n\nOption 3) **22 ∶ 462**\n\n**→ 22 × (22 - 1) **\n\n**→ 22 × 21 = 462.**\n\nOption 4) 13 ∶ 239\n\n→ 13 × (13 - 1) \n\n→ 13 × 12 = 156 ≠ 239.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".\n\n50:Tf92,",
